course: dictionary
lesson: 5059
title: Inside: place, feeling and more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Inside» tells you where something is: in something, within its walls or edges. In «The toy is inside the box», the word after inside, the box, is your clue.
explain: Inside can also show movement. «Let's go inside» means into a building, so here inside works like an adverb. Ask yourself: is the sentence showing a place, or a movement into one?
explain: Inside can point to feelings too. «Inside, she felt nervous» means she felt nervous in her mind, even if she looked calm on the outside. The word inside is not always about a box or a room.
fact: Inside means in something, within its walls or edges.
fact: As an adverb, inside means in or into a building: «Let's go inside.»
fact: The inside of something is its inner part or surface.
fact: «Inside out» means with the inner side turned to the outside.
fact: Inside can also mean in your mind or feelings: «Inside, she felt nervous.»
exercise: «The toy is inside the box.» What does inside mean here? | Very loudly | *In something, within its walls | Outside, on the top of the box | Under the table
exercise: «Let's go inside, it is starting to rain.» What does inside mean here? | Very quickly | *Into a building | Out in the rain | Under the bed
exercise: «Short answers like "whatever" can be about how someone feels inside.» What does inside mean here? | In a box | *In their mind or feelings | In a cupboard | At the edge of a field
test: «The sock was turned inside out.» What does inside out mean? | With the outer side covered in dirt | *With the inner side turned to the outside | Wet through | Brand new and clean
test: «An open oven door and the inside of the oven are hot enough to burn skin.» What is the inside of the oven? | Its outside wall | Its wheels | *Its inner part | Its shiny handle
exam: «Inside the huddle it can be more than 20 degrees warmer than outside.» What does inside the huddle mean? | *Within the middle of the huddle, among the penguins | Far away on the land | Under the sea ice | Outside the huddle at the cold edge
